cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Clack, please cite it as below."
title: "Clack: an acoustic side-channel security auditor"
abstract: >-
  Clack is a defensive auditing tool that measures how vulnerable a keyboard
  environment is to microphone-based keystroke inference, demonstrates the
  leakage live, applies an acoustic countermeasure, and quantitatively verifies
  the reduction (the AUDIT to ATTACK to DEFENSE to VERIFY loop).
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Clack team"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - acoustic side channel
  - keystroke inference
  - security audit
  - defensive security
  - keyboard acoustics
